<title>JAPAN: Sony hits 10,000 yen in Tokyo trade.</title>
<headline>Sony hits 10,000 yen in Tokyo trade.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp shares rose to 10,000 yen on Friday on the Tokyo stock exchange, reaching a new record high, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0011 GMT, the shares had slipped back a touch and were trading up 140 yen at 9,980 yen.</p>
<p>Brokers said investors were relieved that the yen was showing signs of stabilising against the dollar and were growing confident again about exporter issues, especially those in the high technology sector.</p>
</text>
